+## 2026-10-25 reviewer finding: least-frequency row-color rival
+
+A source-bound probe found an unlisted query-changing rival. Every generated
+mixed row has shape `[head, decoy, decoy, ...]`, so the canonical first nonzero
+value is also the unique least-frequent nonzero color. Therefore the rule “emit
+the least frequent nonzero row color, breaking ties by first occurrence” matches
